# WS3-07. Sources: spec/01-lexical.md §2 (legal identifiers) and spec/17-codegen.md §7
# (a local keeps its source name only when it is a valid, unique C identifier) and §1
# (the emitted unit must be valid C99 on every leg). These names are macros, typedefs,
# or globals in the C library, the NDK headers, or the shim; the program must build
# and print 120 on every profile.
profiles: host hosted-amiga hosted-amiga-13
expect: output
contrast: let TRUE: i32 = 1; ==> let TRUE: i32 = 2;
contrast-expect: output
--- output
120
--- contrast-output
121
